SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Ioannis Spiliotis at the Cave
LOCATION:Agios Ioannis (Cave of Antiparos)\, Antiparos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The chapel of Agios Ioannis at the mouth of the famous cave celebrates St John the Theologian on 8 May\, with vespers on the 7th and a panigiri on the terrace outside: traditional dances\, kerasmata\, local dishes and wine. It is Antiparos's best-known feast and a rare chance to be at the cave with locals rather than tour groups.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/antiparos/#agios-ioannis-cave-of-antiparos-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-sp
